WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
SpaceX targets the first upper stage catch on starship flight 15 for November 13th, advancing full

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:13.060
rapid reuse of both stages. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 153, blue origins new third stage,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.040
the south haven compute sites, and cursors live app builder come next, then the engineering

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:24.700
deep dive. Vice President of launch, Kiko Donchev announced at the UP.SUMMIT, Tesla Roddy reports

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.620
that the mission will attempt to catch both the super heavy booster and the ship with the tower arms.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.760
Booster 22 completed a full-duration 33-engine static fire on October 25th.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:41.700
Ship 42 completed a single-engine d-orbit simulation on October 26th and a full six-engine

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.120
static fire the next day.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:48.440
The hardware has finished its test campaign and the pad two arms have already lifted ship

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.080
42 into catch position.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.300
On the third quarter earnings call, Elon Musk said a successful ship catch was more likely

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:55.880
than not.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:02.360
The Starlink constellation that Starship is meant to expand stands at 11,214 satellites

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:07.600
in orbit and 11,200 working out of 13,096 launched.

00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:13.405
Blue Origin Chief Executive Dave Limpe has unveiled a third stage for New Glenn and a

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:16.265
new booster engine in coverage from NASA Space Flight.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:22.145
The GS-3 stage targets direct geostationary orbit injection and Earth escape trajectories,

00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:28.305
rated on the 7x2 vehicle for up to 8 metric tons to geostationary orbit, and 10 metric

00:01:28.305 --> 00:01:34.785
tons to trans-looner injection, and on the larger 9x4 variant for 14 metric tons to geostationary

00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:37.865
orbit, and 20 metric tons to trans-looner injection.

00:01:38.425 --> 00:01:44.725
The North Star engine, burning liquid oxygen and liquefied natural gas, produces 715,000

00:01:44.725 --> 00:01:50.585
pounds of thrust, and GS3 is already under contract for a government sys-looner mission in 2028.

00:01:50.585 --> 00:01:55.765
The stage is not required for Blue Origin's lunar land or architecture, but the company

00:01:55.765 --> 00:01:58.585
says it can support sustained operations around the moon.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:04.485
New Glenn has already flown as a two-stage vehicle from Launch Complex 36 at Cape Canaveral,

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:10.685
and after NG4 was destroyed in a pad explosion during a static fire attempt in May, Blue Origin

00:02:10.685 --> 00:02:15.005
is preparing to return to flight with NG4.1 early in 2027.

00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:21.241
South Haven Action News 5 reports will get two more AI data centers from SpaceX AI.

00:02:21.781 --> 00:02:27.181
The sites expand the company's Memphis area compute footprint alongside the existing Colossus cluster.

00:02:27.841 --> 00:02:32.341
Cursor now lets users describe a tool, then has the agent write it with a database,

00:02:32.761 --> 00:02:36.841
run security checks, and deploy it behind a shareable link the company said.

00:02:37.341 --> 00:02:42.541
The feature is on all paid plans, and teams there are already using the app builder for dashboards,

00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:48.021
words, customer presentations, internal ops tools, onboarding programs, and developer

00:02:48.021 --> 00:02:48.681
portals.

00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:54.166
Charger DeFaire's Denise Sienic said Kiev has started negotiations with the Pentagon

00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:56.126
on a follow-on Starsheel agreement.

00:02:56.826 --> 00:03:03.046
Romanceke reports, the current contract expires around mid-2027, and Ukraine has relied on

00:03:03.046 --> 00:03:05.926
Starsheel for drone operations against Russian threats.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:11.606
Sienic said Kiev is also developing domestic capabilities and looking at European systems,

00:03:11.606 --> 00:03:17.146
and a new agreement must be negotiated, funded, and signed before that mid-2027 date.

00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:24.099
An estimate published by Zeno Spectrum places Colossus 2 storage capacity above 5.2 exabytes

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:28.019
as the cluster scales toward 1.2 million GPUs.

00:03:28.479 --> 00:03:32.839
The figure supports checkpoint and recovery operations across the expanding training and

00:03:32.839 --> 00:03:33.779
inference workload.

00:03:34.299 --> 00:03:39.639
The United States has proposed changes to commercial space launch regulations, Reuters reports,

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:43.699
that could ease licensing for reusable vehicles and higher flight rates.

00:03:44.179 --> 00:03:48.819
The proposal arrives as SpaceX prepares for increased starship operations from multiple

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:49.299
sites.

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:55.359
Kennedy Space Center saw SpaceX complete a full-water day-louge test at Starship Pad 39A,

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:59.619
Basinor reports, in support of future starship operations there.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:06.259
SpaceX is developing two launch pads at Launch Complex 37 at Cape Canaveral, and may be authorized

00:04:06.259 --> 00:04:11.519
to carry out up to 76 starship launches and 152 landings annually from there.

00:04:12.179 --> 00:04:17.119
In the same past, Texas State Representative Gina Hinojosa clicked to Houston reports,

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:22.959
asked Texas Parks and Wildlife to hold off on Boca Chica land action amid SpaceX concerns.

00:04:23.719 --> 00:04:28.979
DeSoto County officials want higher buyout offers from SpaceX AI for properties near plan data

00:04:28.979 --> 00:04:35.139
center sites. The DeSoto Times reports, Voyager 2 has now spent eight years in interstellar space

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:41.299
at roughly 119 astronomical units, with its plasma science experiment still returning data

00:04:41.299 --> 00:04:46.619
until it was powered down last year. Worth keeping an eye on is that no explanation has yet

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:51.839
been received for October speed restrictions that disrupted drone operations, breaking defense

00:04:51.839 --> 00:04:57.619
reports, leaving officials without answers from the Pentagon or SpaceX. No effective alternative

00:04:57.619 --> 00:05:04.369
currently exists, so another gap remains possible if the follow-on is not in place. Catching the ship

00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:09.109
ship on the way back from orbit is the engineering reality of intercepting a vehicle that has already

00:05:09.109 --> 00:05:14.889
survived a full orbital reentry at roughly 25 times the speed of sound. Unlike the super

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:19.189
heavy booster, which separates in the upper atmosphere and returns with modest heating,

00:05:19.609 --> 00:05:25.049
the ship must dissipate the kinetic energy of an entire orbital velocity change, manage peak

00:05:25.049 --> 00:05:30.189
heat fluxes across its windward tiles, and then execute a precise cross-range maneuver

00:05:30.189 --> 00:05:34.989
over to the tower. Per kilogram of returning vehicle, that energy is on the order of

00:05:34.989 --> 00:05:41.309
30 megajoules, a back of envelope figure from 1.5 meters v-squared at about 7.8 kilometers

00:05:41.309 --> 00:05:47.189
per second, which sits near 25 times the speed of sound if you take air at about 340 meters

00:05:47.189 --> 00:05:53.089
per second. Kinetic energy scales with velocity squared, so a full orbital return is a different

00:05:53.089 --> 00:05:58.069
thermal job from a booster's suborbital arc, and the tiles have to finish that job before

00:05:58.069 --> 00:06:03.489
the tower is even in play. The design therefore trades added thermal protection mass and a more

00:06:03.489 --> 00:06:08.009
robust control system for recovering the stage that actually delivers payload to orbit.

00:06:08.689 --> 00:06:13.309
Throttle and gimbal authority on the upper stage engines is what the flight control team needs

00:06:13.309 --> 00:06:18.929
for final alignment once heating drops. If the catch succeeds, the ship no longer needs a separate

00:06:18.929 --> 00:06:24.409
landing site or a recovery vessel, collapsing turnaround from weeks to days and multiplying how

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:27.149
many orbital flights a single ship can perform per year?

00:06:27.709 --> 00:06:32.309
The lever on marginal costs per kilogram once propellant and ground operations dominate

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:32.889
the ledger.

00:06:33.629 --> 00:06:38.169
Liquid oxygen and methane, as a rough order of magnitude, cost a few hundred dollars

00:06:38.169 --> 00:06:43.789
per ton, so the idiot index, how many times a delivered kilogram costs over those raw inputs?

00:06:44.409 --> 00:06:47.689
Only compresses when the ship itself is caught and flown again in days.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:51.729
Blue origins North Star engine illustrates the other mass budget.

00:06:51.729 --> 00:06:57.989
it. An oxygen-rich, staged combustion cycle, described as 30% lighter with 50% fewer

00:06:57.989 --> 00:07:05.189
parts than the BE4, more than 65% 3D printed, and assembled in under a day. Adding a third

00:07:05.189 --> 00:07:10.629
stage opens high energy missions that two-stage vehicles cannot serve efficiently, yet it also

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:15.309
adds recovery and turnaround complexity that catching both the super-heavy booster and the

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:18.949
ship is meant to avoid. Shares sat about 9% lower.

00:07:18.949 --> 00:07:24.653
Before we go, watch that November window for whether the pad two arms take a live super

00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:26.273
heavy booster and a live ship.

